# Class: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit> (Unit)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit> "Unit")
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit> "A unit of measure, or unit, is a particular quantity value that has been chosen as a scale for measuring other quantities the same kind (more generally of equivalent dimension). 
For example, the meter is a quantity of length that has been rigorously defined and standardized by the BIPM (International Board of Weights and Measures).  Any measurement of the length can be expressed as a number multiplied by the unit meter. 
More formally, the value of a physical quantity Q with respect to a unit (U) is expressed as the scalar multiple of a real number (n) and U, as  $Q = nU$."@en)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> (Material)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> "Instances of Portions Of Matter whose shape is relevant for their dispostion to participate in a manufacturing process may be (subclasses of) objects that bear a 'blank role' in the context of the manufacturing process."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> "Material is defined in terms of the three main perspectives that material specifications rely on: the structure of the material (\"intensive quality\"), the performance of the material (\"behavoiral material property\") and the processing the material must have undergone (\"output of some process\").

When defining specific materials/material taxonomies, these three aspects shall be taken into account in the aristotelian (\"per genus et differentiam\") as differentiation."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> "The sum of portions of matter of the same type form a portion of matter of that type."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> "Material"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> "material"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:altLabel <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> "Portion of Material"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> "A material is a portion of matter that may participate in some manufacturing process and whose shape is not relevant for its participation in the manufacturing process."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:BFO_0000017) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:BFO_0000019) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002353 obo:BFO_0000015)))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> (portion of matter)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> "It is also representing a distinct physical or conceptual part of a material or substance.

The open energy ontology OEO defines portion of matter as a subclass of object aggregate, which implies countability. Our portion is not (precisely) countable and thus bearer of intensive properties."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> "Lome explanation for portion of matter: \"What is a molecule cluster at the cellular level? Contrary to the molecular level, at the cellular level of granularity the boundary of each molecule is outside of the level of granular focus. What forms a discontinuous cluster of countable individual molecules and thus bona fide objects at the molecular level, is a continuous and non-countable molecular substance at coarser levels of
granularity. At these coarser levels, the individual molecules cannot be differentiated and demarcated anymore and the cluster as a whole possesses only fiat inner boundaries.\""@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> "portion of matter"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> "A material entity that is not demarcated by any physical discontinuities. At some finer level of granularity it is an object aggregate, at some coarser level of granularity it is a fiat object part,but at this level of granularity it is neither."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> obo:BFO_0000040)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> (engineered material)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> "We recognize that some of the materials in the subclasses also occur naturally. However, these are not within the scope of our consideration for technical use."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> "engineered material"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> "material that is output of a manufacturing process"@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:OBI_0000312 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833>)))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:OBI_0000312 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> (Materialeigenschaft)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> "A property is a material trait in terms of the kind and magnitude of response to a specific imposed stimulus. Generally, definitions of properties are made independent of material shape and size.
(Callister, W.D., Rethwisch, D.G., Materials Science and Engineering, Wiley, 2014)

Technical materials are complex aggregates. Many properties that are determined for those aggregates are intrinsically associated with the methodologies employed in the measurement process. This is in contrast to typical 'physical' properties, which like e.g. mass that can be determined to high accuracy independently of the measurement process. 
As a consequence, material properties in the ontology are differeciated according to their measurement method, e.g. Brinell hardness and Vickers hardness are different types of indentation hardness rather than different measures/quantification (GDC) of the materials property 'indentation hardness'.
 The 'unit idenifieres' of such properties (e.g. \"HV1\", \"HV10\", \"HBW\") are strictly speaking not units but rather references to the measurement methodology used to determine a numeric value that quantifies the property.

Extensive properties that depend on the object being tested rather than on the portion of matter are (extensive) object- or system-properties."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> "Materialeigenschaft"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> "material performance property"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> "a disposition of a portion of matter that is realized in a compatible process and whose realization is grounded in the portions intensive qualities"@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020353>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0023004>)
SubClassOf(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Due to the duality of object and portion of matter this axiom can not be an equivalent class axiom."@en) <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000052 ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000056 obo:BFO_0000015))))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> (process attribute)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> "Process attribute for a process has a similar application to specifically dependened continuant (SDC) for an independent continuant (IC). Furthermore, process attribute describes how SDCs of some participants, i.e., ICs, change in a process. 

Specific rates, e.g., tensile rate, cooling rate, etc. should be added as  subclasses of this class."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> "process attribute"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:altLabel <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> "process characteristic"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> "a process attribute is a dependent occurrent that existentially depends on a process."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:example <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> "Tensile rate in a tensile testing process. Cooling rate in a quenching process"@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> obo:BFO_0000003)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025006> obo:BFO_0000015))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000068> (temporally qualified continuant)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000068> "temporally qualified continuant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000068> "A temporally qualified continuant is a continuant that, by reference to a determinate temporal region, is such as to possess its properties only for so long as that period obtains, being otherwise in its essentiality unchanged."@en)
