# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> (chemical reaction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> "chemical reaction"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> "chemische Reaktion"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> "Das Auftreten einer chemischen Reaktion ist der Prozess, bei dem Substanzen interagieren, um neue chemische Verbindungen zu bilden oder ihre Molekülstruktur zu verändern."@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> "The occurrence of (a) chemical reaction is the process in which substances interact to form new chemical compounds or alter their molecular structure."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869> obo:BFO_0000015)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> (optical property)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> "optical property"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> "optische Eigenschaft"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> "a property that is commonly associated with the domain of optics"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:example <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> "A camera lens has an optical capability of resolving 100 line pairs per mm at the image plane"@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020265>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000882> (Phasengrenze (Realisierung))

