# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> (OBSOLETE bravais lattice (3D))

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "TODO: possibly extend for 2D (Graphene etc)

More elaborate crystal descriptions may be found in http://emmo.info/domain-crystallography/crystallography or https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/disos/cso"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "Bravais-Gitter (3D)"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "OBSOLETE bravais lattice (3D)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "Das Bravais-Gitter ist eine kategoriale Wertspezifikation, die den Wert der Kristallstrukturqualität angibt. Es beschreibt die mögliche geometrische Anordnung von Gitterpunkten in einem Kristall. Der vorliegende Deskriptor beschränkt sich auf die 14 möglichen dreidimensionalen Anordnungen."@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "The bravais lattice is a categorical value specification that specifies value of the crystal structure quality. It describes the possible geometric arrangement of lattice points in a crystal. The present descriptor is limited to the 14 possible three-dimensional arrangements."@en)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> (fraction property)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> "Concentrations can be expressed in terms of three quantifiers:

+-------------------+------------------+-------------------+---------------------+
---------------------+
|                   | count            | mass              | volume              |
 length                  |  area
+-------------------+------------------+-------------------+---------------------+
| per count         | molar fraction  | -------  |-------  |
 ------ | ------
| per mass          | count per mass   | mass per mass     | volume per mass     |
 ------- | ---------
| per volume        | count per volume | mass per volume   | volume per volume   |
| per length         | length number density  |-------  | ------ | length fraction | --------
| per area          |  area number density  |-------  | ------ | -------- | area fraction
+-------------------+------------------+-------------------+---------------------+

Mass per count and volume per count are not known to have practical examples but are included for completeness."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> "Kamilla:
1.  concentration is a bad name, cause area fraction (texture component or phase on the image) is also relationship between part and the whole.
2. Number desity (of precipitates) can be the same as count per volume or count per area or count per length. How to deal with that?"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> "Ratio: 
A comparison of two or more quantities (a relationship), e.g. 3:2:1 for prosecco, aperol and sparkling water in aperol spritz. There is no stanardized mathematical notation or operators for it.  We do not support it, rather convert it to fractions.

Proportion: 
A statement that two ratios/fractions are equal (an equation), e.g. 2/3=4/6"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> "fraction property"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:altLabel <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> "part-whole property"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> "a property describing a quantitative relation between two entites where one entity represents the whole and the other entity represents a part of the whole"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:example <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> "aperol spritz: 3/6 prosecco, 2/6 aperol, 1/6 sparkling water in vol/vol"@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> ObjectIntersectionOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002503 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:BFO_0000004 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:BFO_0000004))) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025999> obo:BFO_0000004)))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020108>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002503 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:BFO_0000004 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:BFO_0000004))))

