# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> (elastische Deformation)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> "elastic strain"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> "elastische Deformation"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:altLabel <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> "elastic deformation"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:altLabel <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> "elastische Verformung"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> "Bei der elastischen Dehnung handelt es sich um eine Dehnungsqualität eines Materialgebildes, die durch eine reversible Verformung gekennzeichnet ist, die bei Wegnahme der aufgebrachten Last verschwindet"@de)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> "Elastic strain is a strain quality of a material entity characterized by reversible deformation that disappears upon removal of the applied load"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:example <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> "Steel loaded to 200 MPa exhibits an elastic strain of about 0.001, fully recovered upon unloading"@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080034> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080029>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080050> (entropy)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080050> "SI unit: joules per kelvin (J/K)

Statistical definition (Boltzmann):
S=k_B ln(W)
where k_B​ is the Boltzmann constant and W is the number of microstates."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080050> "entropy"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080050> "Entropy is a measure of the disorder or randomness of a system — more precisely, the number of microscopic arrangements (microstates) consistent with the system's macroscopic state."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080050> ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020142> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000080 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020128>)))

