# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080116> (potential)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080116> "Every potential in physics is the same mathematical object — a partial derivative of energy with respect to its conjugate extensive quantity. The differences are only in which extensive quality you're considering."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080116> "potential"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080116> "a partial derivative of energy with respect to its conjugate extensive quantity"@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080116> obo:BFO_0000019)
SubClassOf(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In field theories (e.g., gravity, electrostatics), the potential becomes a field ϕ(r⃗), and the force is recovered via:
F=−∇ϕ(r⃗)F
This is the spatial analogue: instead of asking \"how does energy change per unit carrier added?\", you ask \"how does energy change per unit carrier moved in space?\""@en) <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0080116> ObjectIntersectionOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002328 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020142>) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002328 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020319>)))

